{"kind":"request","text":"Join parity, head JP1: one invite parser and one rule for Start,\nthe CLI and MCP\n\nRuling on 9719b634. Join parity is part of the stable base. I\naccept inventory fe579da3. Order act fc7576f8 left the question\nopen, and this request answers it. C1 and M1a are parked, so the\norder line of 9719b634 no longer applies. The work takes two heads.\n\nHead JP1 (this request) opens now as a parallel lane. It changes\nhow a person link is read, and nothing else.\n\n1. Keep one person-invite parser in packages/client. Delete the\n   other one. Today the CLI and the page use browser-helpers.ts:95,\n   and MCP uses client invitation.ts:21. Say which one stays and\n   why. Account for the public export at client index.ts:15 and\n   for browser-joining.ts:9.\n\n2. One rule for the Membership pin. Every surface requires the\n   explicit pin, as the page does at data.ts:304. Remove the\n   fallback to Membership@1 at commands.ts:604 and service.ts:1499.\n   Report each shipped fixture, document or invitation writer that\n   produces a link without the pin, and correct it in this head.\n\n3. One rule for the service. Every surface accepts a trailing\n   slash, as the page does at data.ts:306. MCP stops comparing the\n   raw strings at service.ts:1497.\n\n4. Add no tagged receiver and no check mode in this head.\n\nWitness: one table of person links, each row given to the entry\nfunction of each surface. The rows are a valid link, a link with\nno pin, a link with a trailing slash on the service, a link for\nanother service, and a malformed link. The three surfaces give the\nsame answer on every row. The witness runs locally and needs no\nroom.\n\nHead JP2 comes after identifiers head (c+d) and the cutover\nfamily, because both change the invitation and membership shapes.\nI file its request when (c+d) is in review. Its content, so that\nJP1 leaves room for it:\n- MCP join accepts a tagged agent invitation. It runs the judge\n  that CLI enrolment runs at invitations.ts:443 to 576, moved to\n  a shared module and not copied.\n- MCP join gains a check mode that answers as `dap join --check`\n  answers.\n- Checker and device invitations stay with the CLI and the page.\n  The documents name that limit.\n- Item 3 of 9719b634 and its membership witnesses land here.\n\nJP1 takes the gate slot after head F. Checker review at the exact\nhead. No builder deployment.","body":{"conditions":"One person-invite parser in packages/client used by Start, the CLI and MCP; every surface requires the explicit Membership pin and accepts a trailing slash on the service; the duplicate parser and the Membership@1 fallback are deleted; one table witness gives the same answer on all three surfaces. Gate at the head, checker review, no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}